{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Reduce long service medal qualifying periods from 20 to 15 years",
        "additional_details": "Those serving in our Ambulance, Fire and Rescue, Police and Prison Services dedicate their careers to protecting the public, often working in challenging and dangerous conditions. Their commitment deserves recognition. Reducing the qualifying period to 15 years, with further bars at 25, 35 and 45 years, would recognise their dedication and bring their long-service awards into closer alignment with those of their Armed Forces colleagues.",
        "background": "We want the Government to seek to reduce the qualifying period for Ambulance, Fire and Rescue, Police and Prison Services Long Service Medals from 20 to 15 years, with a bar awarded for every additional 10 years of qualifying service, in line with Armed Forces colleagues.",
